WEBVTT

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.580
People arbitrarily assign value to things and then treasure them.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.990
But as time passes, these objects become vessels for lost souls,

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.440
and become what we call “artificial spirits”.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.740
This is a tale of people under the spell of such beings.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.820
A man sold his pocket watch, and bought a brush for his wife.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.780
The wife sold her beautiful hair to buy her husband a chain for his pocket watch.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.450
What a sweet story.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.880
I wish my work here was that exciting.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.430
Those kinds of things only happen in books, I guess.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.680
Welcome.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.590
I'd like to sell this, please.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.240
This is a beautiful vase.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.640
But I can't afford to pay that much for it.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.990
Any price is fine.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.240
I'd be more than happy to just get rid of it.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:00.990
Thanks for your business!

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:07.580
Hey, that's—

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.590
Pardon me, but did my wife sell a vase to you?

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.460
I did purchase one from a woman yesterday.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.680
I knew it! How dare she sell off MY collection!

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.510
How much is it? I'll pay whatever you ask!

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.010
Thanks for your business!

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.620
Sorry to trouble you, but would you please take this off my hands again?

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.110
Sure, thanks a bunch.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.480
Excuse me! Please sell me that vase!

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.280
'Preciate it!

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.660
I'd like to sell this!

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.490
Sure thing.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.240
I'll take it!

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:41.700
You got it.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.800
I can't take this anymore!

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.990
Please see to it that this vase is sold far, far away!

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:48.560
HEY!

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.330
D-Dear!

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.840
Quit screwing with my collection!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.170
Quit obsessing over this piece of crap!

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.300
It's a free country, dammit!

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.560
How much money have you wasted on this!?

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.050
It's the money I'VE earned!

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.990
Can't you try so see things my way!?

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.060
No! I'm not backing down!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.310
What do you love more, me or this stupid vase!?

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.720
Anyway, I'm taking this home with me!

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:09.850
Keep your mouth shut, woman!

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.740
Let's see, that was five round trips, so here's what you owe.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.270
It's said that everyone has their own special talent.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:00.860
But there are many who go their whole lives unable to find it.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:07.260
Those who do realize their gifts however, may simply be blessed with good fortune.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:08.440
Sanada!

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:09.340
Got it!

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.650
Gorilla!

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.090
Is that supposed to mean me!?

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:28.650
Don't just make up nicknames on the spot!

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.080
Sorry, man.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.690
Asai, you idiot! What are you doing!?

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.960
Don't make Sanada-kun look bad!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.790
What'cha looking at?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.490
Oh, the boys, huh?

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:42.180
I wish that was <i>our</i> test.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.020
So, who's winning?

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.040
Huh?

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.630
Umm, good question.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.670
Weren't you watching the game?

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:50.970
Okay, nice job!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.980
All right, next... Arashiyama!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.620
Yes ma'am!

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.530
Ahh! Coach!

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:13.020
Don't stand right in front of the landing mat! That's dangerous!

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.690
Look behind you, Arashiyama.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.030
BEHIND YOU!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:18.880
Huh?

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.460
Did I warp or something?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.730
You're not extending your left arm fully, so you can't dismount properly.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.220
Okay, you're free to go play ping-pong.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.370
What the heck are you doing?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.220
Just checking to see if the space here is distorted or not.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:36.230
“Careless Miss” and “Hairless Miss” sound similar.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.910
Finished your test, Tattsun?

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.130
Yup. A perfect landing, naturally.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.690
Ta-da! Let's play some ping-pong!

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.860
You and me?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.910
Well, why not?

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.910
Starbucks and Star Tours sound similar.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.580
Guess I could humor her for a bit.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.200
Here goes!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.050
What?

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.310
Here.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.090
Hey—

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.970
I'm pretty good, huh?

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.310
Yup. You've got a gift.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.970
Take that!  Man, I'm good!

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.600
You think I'm a prodigy?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.480
Well, do ya?

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.230
I'm just going easy on... YOU!

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:32.380
My quick visual reflexes can easily spot the fast-approaching sphere...

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.700
However!

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:40.500
Whether or not I can react in time is a different matter all together.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:46.680
That spike... you haven't lost your touch at all, Tatsuno-san.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.090
Haribara-san...

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.070
There, there.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.980
That was mean! It really hurt!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.940
It was spherical!

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.770
The shape has nothing to do with it.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.330
How about a match for old times' sake?

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.560
Arashiyama-san's not even a challenge for you.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.530
HEY!  I was using this tab—

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:08.410
Unbelievable!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:12.250
I never thought I'd witness a match between South Middle #3's twin aces!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.180
OW! What the hell!?

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.870
I was also in the ping-pong club back then.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.960
But now, I'm in the film club.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:26.260
They were feared as the Faerie and Reaper of South Middle #3!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.050
So what about Kon-senpai, then?

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.430
She went to the same school, right?

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:38.930
Kon Futaba...

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:44.160
It's said that the villagers froze in their tracks upon hearing the name...

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.440
What villagers!?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.150
She-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named was a whole different beast.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.240
The demoness of South Middle #3...

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.990
A.K.A. Satan incarnate...

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.620
or even Darth Vader...

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.700
The Sith Lord!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.400
She had many fearsome nicknames.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.610
Only such names could truly describe her ridiculous strength.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.210
She's that good, huh?

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.470
Tatsuno-san opens with a killer serve!

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.730
Whoa! It's like the pro matches on TV!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:31.690
She's good. Tatsuno-san's not your average player!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.820
You wouldn’t guess she hasn’t played in over a year!

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:39.610
Impossible! Her biggest weakness, her footwork, has been corrected!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:42.450
She's not getting tired!

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.710
Mind if I start playing seriously?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.900
This reminds me of middle school.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.260
I'm starting to enjoy this!

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.220
I've been going all-out from the start!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.980
That stance!

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.480
Is she going to do it?

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.180
Do what?

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.600
There it is!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.880
Haribara Special: The Reaper's Scythe!

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.450
Special!? Reaper's Scythe!?

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:15.360
Ever since one student fell and was
knocked unconscious trying to chase it,

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.520
it's been called The Reaper's Scythe...

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:19.930
...by me!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.350
You just made it up!?

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.390
Now... time to die!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.010
She returned it!

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.720
But Tattsun's lost her balance and can't recover in time!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.010
You're mine!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.260
I win! I've defeated Tatsuno Toshiko!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:43.700
I'm gonna lose!

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.800
Sanada-kun's watching me...

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:51.770
I will not...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.820
...be defeated!

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:04.330
Okay, pack it up, guys!

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.830
My whole body aches.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.840
So who won, anyway?

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.130
I don't really get the rules and stuff.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.880
I lost. There's no way I could've beaten someone who still plays.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.570
Hmm... learned something new today.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.640
When I become a genius detective,

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:29.850
my job will be finding out who the perp is, not catching him.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.610
So why would I need stupid gymnastics skills?

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.090
You too, Tattsun.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.740
If you're gonna be Sanada's wife, who cares about ping-pong?

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.970
You've been making fun of me this whole time, haven't you?

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:49.970
Or are you trying to console me?

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.170
Your heart is a black hole of emotion!

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.170
I've always been “good” at everything, but never “great”.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.610
I mastered the basics of stuff like the violin and ping-pong no problem.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:05.770
I could make it pretty far with almost no effort.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.600
But then I hit a wall,

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:11.190
And the truly hardworking geniuses overtake me.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:13.840
I'm forever doomed to be second-rate.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.070
Go on and laugh...

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.900
I can't tell if you're tough or a coward.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:23.730
It's said that everyone has their own special talent.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:27.870
But there are many who go their whole lives unable to find it.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:32.170
But the truly perceptive can find it where they stand out.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.830
Did you see that match, Sanada?

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:35.710
Yeah.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.890
She's in a class all her own, huh?

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.920
Shake... Shake...

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.930
They were like water balloons... her boobs.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:44.970
Don't say that.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:46.930
It's unbecoming.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.850
A portrait of the sun.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.250
Year 2, Class A. Sanada Hiroyuki.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:57.100
Now, let us merely observe the sunset in silence.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.760
Burning its shaking image...

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.940
...into our hearts.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.770
Nothing is impossible if you persevere.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.330
Even the most difficult of endeavors.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:10.960
Unrelenting quests, fueled by strong emotion, have changed the course of history...

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.960
And made dreams into reality.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.210
People call these phenomena “miracles”.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.090
Welcome.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.840
I thought I'd grab a bite before I head home.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:30.100
Thank you. We'll be closing the shop at the end of the month, unfortunately.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:34.320
My mother and I really loved these...

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.820
I guess the colors turn most people off from them...

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.560
They're just not selling well enough.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.280
It can't be true! I can't imagine life without these.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.040
I'll take every single thing in this store!

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:19.650
This is delicious!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:22.210
Hey grandpa...

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:24.650
What were those multi-colored snacks from Mori's?

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:25.900
Huh?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.790
Huh? Oh, some passing stranger gave it to me.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.040
Did you eat one?

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.900
Nope. He only gave me one.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:38.410
There's no way I'd eat something that nasty lookin'.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:42.250
I've never heard of Rainbow Delights before.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.550
Have you, grandpa?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.550
Ah, come to think of it, didn't I see those back in the day?

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.390
Nope.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.630
Maybe the convenience store has them.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:01.620
If they do, I'll clean 'em out tomorrow.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.570
Did you eat breakfast today, Senpai?

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.190
Yeah.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:14.470
You wouldn't shut up about it, so I wolfed down a
processed, fat-ladened hunk of bread this morning.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:18.460
Why do you have to have such an attitude about it?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.600
Shizuka-neechan, up early? Now that's a rare sight.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.460
Yeah, I guess.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.220
You girls ever heard of Rainbow Delights?

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.430
Rainbow Delights? No, I haven’t.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:34.620
So it's not one of those new kids’ snacks...

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.140
What is it? Is it good?

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.700
It's really good.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.650
It's blue, pink, and bright green...

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.780
Crunchy, but soft and chewy too.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.530
Is it actual food?

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.870
I went to three different stores, and none of them had it.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.870
“Love Letter” and “Predator” sound similar.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:56.620
Maybe it's from one of the mom and pop places.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.390
“Mori's”, hmm?

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.130
I wonder if I can order some.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.890
The number you have dialed is not in service.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.070
Please hang up and try a—

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:15.140
It hadn't expired yet either... right?

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.390
That's really strange.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.250
That's ridiculous...

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:44.980
There's no city by that name in C prefecture.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.500
I've never heard of it before either.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:51.510
What's going on? Why the phony address?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:58.260
Some passing stranger gave it to me.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:02.560
“Gave” seems like my only clue.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:08.020
At the very least, this mysterious third party isn't made up.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.290
A city that doesn't exist.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.000
An unused telephone number.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:31.050
The only lead this fake packaging offers is an out-of-city zip code.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.030
The zip code is used in C prefecture.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:41.270
Guess I'll ride around the area and check all the confectioneries.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:43.270
Here's your eel bowl.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.230
Umm, excuse me...

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:48.360
Yes?

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:52.720
Would you happen to know of a confectionary called “Mori's” around here?

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:56.680
A candy store, or a Japanese treats store kind of place.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.300
Don't tell me, Rainbow Delights?

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.940
You're the third person to ask me.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:05.920
You're asking if it's made somewhere around these parts, aren't you?

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.990
Sorry, but I've never heard of it.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.260
You from Tokyo, dear?

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:17.010
Must be something if you've come all this way for some.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.100
I'm sorry for bothering you this late at night.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.850
Not at all.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.660
I just run the inn on the side,

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.230
so it's not so strange to have guests come by around this time.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.150
I don't have any dinner for you, though.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.150
I ate before coming, so I'll be fine.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.490
By the way, you wouldn't happen to be
familiar with Rainbow Delights, would you?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.990
Hmm?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.030
If you're still hungry, you can have this.

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.230
Here's some hot water.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:49.300
Ogata Ken sounds like Kai Ken.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:55.170
So there's been others who asked
about Rainbow Delights at that shop.

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.090
And both of them are from Tokyo too.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:00.920
I bet they had one as well.

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:02.830
One of those addictive little multi-colored treats...

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.310
They must have eaten one and tried to find more.

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:11.100
Did that man just walk around Tokyo handing them out to people?

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:12.090
But why would he do that?

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:17.620
My mind's buzzing more than it does when I'm writing.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:22.390
Of all the things to be obsessed over...

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.380
Wait, am I just imagining it?

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.660
Did I <i>really</i> eat that?

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:38.970
Please Miss... right this way.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.320
Is this...

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:12.340
Is this Mihasora City?

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.540
I've finally found Mihasora City!

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:20.930
That was close.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.060
I almost wound up in some weird fantasy novel.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.270
That's not it.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:42.180
None of the ingredients written here turn blue or pink even if you fry or bake them.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.410
I know that, but still...

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.530
Are you sure you didn't dream that?

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.290
You went all the way to C prefecture and nobody had it, right?

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.440
This has to be some kind of snack made with futuristic technology.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.130
Excellent deduction, Future Frames!

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.340
I've discovered the secret behind this wrapper!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.140
Who the heck are you calling “Future Frames”!?

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.380
The expiration date only has the last 2 digits of the year, right?

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:09.030
So this isn't from the year 2010...

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:12.400
...but maybe the year 2510 instead!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:17.290
It's totally possible for cities we've never heard of to spring up hundreds of years from now.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:21.240
There you have it, so let's give up on trying to recreate them.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.240
It's just not possible in our time.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:27.470
I've eaten so much that my stomach hurts.

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:28.740
Yeah, me too.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:33.000
First it's fantasy novels, and now it's sci-fi...

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:44.120
You've become the first man to successfully travel through time. How do you feel?

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:47.120
Hard to say. I'm still getting over the time lag.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.270
Now that you're home, what's the first thing you want to do?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.530
I really liked this snack called Rainbow Delights.

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.530
I could sure go for one right about now.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:03.880
That long trip through sub-time gave you a craving for the common man's food, huh?

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:08.370
Common man's food? You've heard of it?

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:12.250
Rainbow Delights, right?

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.460
They sell 'em practically everywhere.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.880
I've got one in my briefcase. If you want it, go right ahead.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.130
If you're fine with just one, you can have mine.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:27.890
With 300 years of determination, miracles can come about.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:35.500
You conducted several experiments during your trip to the 2000's.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.770
How did they turn out?

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:44.250
They were a big success.

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:18.240
Safety-pin sounds like Mandolin.

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:21.120
Welcome.

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:25.380
Hey, Shizuka-san, would you buy this please?

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:29.240
Sure, but you won't get much for it.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:31.260
That's fine. Better than just throwing it out.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:35.380
Hey, does anyone else in your family want this?

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:37.220
If anyone did, I wouldn't be here.

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:38.970
Then I don't either.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:39.890
Why!?

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.960
Do you ever think Macaroni is just the hollow part itself?

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:46.440
I've never once thought that.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:50.470
But that's the best part of it, don't you think?

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:52.980
Now that you mention it, maybe...

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:56.550
If you think about it, your life until now feels kinda empty too, doesn't it?

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.600
The other day, I tried making hole-less macaroni.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.800
How'd it go?

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:03.050
I just ended up with thick spaghetti.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.920
Next time: 10th Street.

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:07.720
The finger-pointing geriatric.

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:11.010
Round and round, all sexy-like.
